DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20250317
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20250318
SUMMARY:California: 565 (partnership) / 568 (LLC) / 100S (S-corp) due
DESCRIPTION:California partnership/LLC/S-corp return due the 15th day of th
 e 3rd month after year-end. California's LLC annual tax/fee (Form 3522/3536
 ) has its own separate due dates\, and CA's PTE elective tax (Form 3893) ha
 s separate payment due dates (June 15 and March 15 of the following year) -
  neither is this base return due date. Correction (this rebuild session): t
 he cited source states the general rule (15th day of the 3rd month) without
  addressing the 2026-specific weekend interaction - March 15\, 2026 is a Su
 nday. Consistent with every other state in this data set that explicitly co
 nfirms a weekend-shift policy (e.g. Massachusetts\, New York\, Vermont\, De
 laware\, Montana\, Oregon all confirm shifting to March 16\, 2026)\, and wi
 th the near-universal US government-deadline convention of shifting to the 
 next business day\, this entry's date_2026 was corrected from an unshifted 
 March 15\, 2026 to March 16\, 2026. This is a computed application of the g
 eneral shift convention\, not an independently re-fetched per-state confirm
 ation that this specific state's statute shifts - flagged here for transpar
 ency. | California partnership/LLC/S-corp return due the 15th day of the 3r
 d month after year-end. California's LLC annual tax/fee (Form 3522/3536) ha
 s its own separate due dates\, and CA's PTE elective tax (Form 3893) has se
 parate payment due dates (June 15 and March 15 of the following year) - nei
 ther is this base return due date. Automatic extension (no separate extensi
 on form required to file)\, but full payment of tax/fee is still due by the
  original date. (100S S-corp extended date is September 15\, one month earl
 ier than the partnership/LLC extended date.) Correction (this rebuild sessi
 on): the cited source states the general rule (15th day of the 3rd month) w
 ithout addressing the 2026-specific weekend interaction - March 15\, 2026 i
 s a Sunday. Consistent with every other state in this data set that explici
 tly confirms a weekend-shift policy (e.g. Massachusetts\, New York\, Vermon
 t\, Delaware\, Montana\, Oregon all confirm shifting to March 16\, 2026)\, 
 and with the near-universal US government-deadline convention of shifting t
 o the next business day\, this entry's date_2026 was corrected from an unsh
 ifted March 15\, 2026 to March 16\, 2026. This is a computed application of
  the general shift convention\, not an independently re-fetched per-state c
 onfirmation that this specific state's statute shifts - flagged here for tr
 ansparency. | Authority: California Franchise Tax Board\, direct fetch this
  session: partnership/LLC due "15th day of the 3rd month after the close of
  your tax year\," extended "15th day of the 10th month"\; S-corp due "15th 
 day of the 3rd month\," extended "15th day of the 9th month." | Source: htt
